      "skill_id": "en-a2-017",
      "title": "Recognizing simple present and past passives",
      "explanation": "In a passive sentence the thing that receives the action is the subject. Form the present passive with am, is or are plus the past participle: English is spoken here. Form the past passive with was or were plus the past participle: The window was broken yesterday. Notices and descriptions often use the passive. Add by to name who did it: The book was written by Orwell.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "English is spoken here."
        },
        {
          "en": "The window was broken yesterday."
        },
        {
          "en": "The book was written by Orwell."
        }
      ],
